# Clinical Data & Vocabularies
data/athena_omop/*
data/snomed_kg/*
data/processed/*
data/medical_abbreviations/*

# MIMIC-IV / PhysioNet-restricted data -- credentialed access only, must
# never be redistributed via a public git repo (data use agreement).
# Deleted from tracking 2026-08-23; ignored here so it can't be
# accidentally re-added later. raw_notes uses the same *-plus-.gitkeep-
# exception pattern as the other clinical-data dirs below (directory
# structure preserved, contents ignored); the SNOMED-CT challenge dir
# never had that convention, so it's ignored outright.
data/raw_notes/*
data/snomed-ct-entity-linking-challenge-1.2.0/

# 2026-08-28: a real local-dev gap found via the Streamlit UI -- with the
# real directories deleted (above), data/raw_notes/* and the trailing-
# slash pattern only match CONTENTS of an actual directory at that path,
# not a symlink placed directly at "data/raw_notes" itself (e.g. one
# pointing at a sibling worktree's real, credentialed-access copy of this
# same PhysioNet data for local testing) -- confirmed live, such a symlink
# showed up as untracked (`??`) rather than ignored, a real risk of it
# getting swept into a careless `git add -A`. These two bare
# (no-trailing-slash) patterns close that gap by matching the path itself
# regardless of type (file, directory, or symlink).
#
# KNOWN, ACCEPTED TRADE-OFF: a bare pattern excludes the directory itself,
# not just its contents, which means git's own documented limitation now
# applies -- a file cannot be re-included by a `!` negation if its parent
# directory is itself excluded. This makes the
# `!data/raw_notes/.gitkeep` exception below permanently inert for
# data/raw_notes specifically (verified empirically; a `!data/raw_notes/`
# directory-negation was tried first and did NOT restore it either).
# Accepted deliberately: compliance (never let this symlink become
# trackable) matters more than the cosmetic convenience of an empty
# tracked directory placeholder, which is what would be lost.
data/raw_notes
data/snomed-ct-entity-linking-challenge-1.2.0

# Exception: Keep the directory structure intact in git
!data/raw_notes/.gitkeep
!data/athena_omop/.gitkeep
!data/snomed_kg/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/medical_abbreviations/.gitkeep
!data/guidelines/.gitkeep

